model time07_reverse
  tally 2
  on 2025-05-31
  start 2025-05-01
  end 2025-05-31
  note "Probe TIME-07, the reverse order the question asks: the 15th rule reads the balance at its day's start, before the pay lands (`bal(konto, rule_day start)`, L §5.14.2: plans come first, so no `before` can put a decision ahead of one). The stated order is TIME-07.tally."

source probe_card "Probe card TIME-07 (made-up story and rules)"

unit DUK: currency minor 0.01

place employer: outside lives 2025-05-01..

place konto: accounts DUK lives 2025-05-01..

place savings: accounts DUK lives 2025-05-01..

input keep_floor: money DUK

input pay_amt: money DUK

input pay_day: date

input rule_day: date

move sweep: transfers
  on rule_day
  reads konto
  leg cash from konto to savings amount max(0, bal(konto, rule_day start) - keep_floor)
  note "rule 1: keep a floor of 2 000.00, move the rest to savings; a decision that reads the balance at the start of its day, before the pay (L §5.14.1, §5.14.2)"

move wage: transfers
  on pay_day
  leg cash from employer to konto amount pay_amt
  note "story: her pay lands on 15 May 2025"

ask q_reverse: flows(sweep, 2025-05-15) law 2025-05-31

version card
  cite probe_card
  governs always
  known 2025-05-01
  note "Stipulations, known from the model's start (L §4.5)."
  keep_floor = 2000.00 "rule 1: keep a floor of 2 000.00"
  opening[konto] = 1500.00 at 2025-05-01 start "story: 1 500.00 before anything happens on 15 May 2025; no movement before it"
  pay_amt = 6000.00 "story: her pay"
  pay_day = 2025-05-15 "story: the pay lands on 15 May 2025"
  rule_day = 2025-05-15 "story: the 15th rule runs that day"
